utomobile products. This segment also offers consumer and commercial products, such as landscape edging; industrial, home, and office matting; marine dock edging; and masonry joint controls. It offers its products to chemical processors; plastics fabricators; small construction contractors; municipalities; and supply warehouses for use in various consumer and industrial markets, including residential construction, flexible and rigid packaging, automotive products, healthcare products, water treatment, wind turbines, and coatings, as well as other durable and non-durable goods. The company was formerly known as Westlake Chemical Corporation and changed its name to Westlake Corporation in February 2022. Westlake Corporation was founded in 1986 and is headquartered in Houston, Texas. Westlake Corporation is a subsidiary of TTWF LP.","employees":14600,"website":"https://www.westlake.com","country":"United States","city":"Houston","officers":[{"name":"Mr. Albert Yuan Chao","title":"Executive Chairman"},{"name":"Mr. James Y. Chao","title":"Senior Chairman"},{"name":"Mr. Jean-Marc  Gilson","title":"President, CEO & Director"}]},"sector_medians":{"fpe":11.94,"tpe":19.13,"ps":2.295,"pfcf":24.77,"peg":1.72,"pb":2.453,"ev_ebitda":9.424,"rev_growth":0.1625,"eps_growth":0.396,"eps_growth_fwd":0.318,"eps_growth_next":0.1474,"div_yield":0.0086,"roe":0.1295,"roa":0.06934,"de":45.45,"gross_margin":0.3315,"op_margin":0.162,"profit_margin":0.08041,"current_ratio":2.244},"valuation":[{"k":"fpe","label":"Forward P/E","v":39.58,"sector":11.94,"verdict":"Overvalued"},{"k":"tpe","label":"TTM P/E","v":-1,"sector":19.13,"verdict":"Loss-making"},{"k":"ps","label":"Price / Sales","v":0.7171,"sector":2.295,"verdict":"Undervalued"},{"k":"pfcf","label":"Price / FCF","v":18.86,"sector":24.77,"verdict":"Undervalued"},{"k":"peg","label":"PEG","v":1.7,"sector":1.72,"verdict":"Fairly valued"},{"k":"pb","label":"Price / Book","v":0.9473,"sector":2.453,"verdict":"Undervalued"},{"k":"de","label":"Debt / 